# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so

# Generated results - committed because they ARE the deliverable. Never hand-edit them;
# re-run the modules to regenerate (see README "How to run").
# The source clip data/conveyor.mp4 is committed too (4 MB, far under GitHub's 100 MB limit) so
# that every number reported here can actually be re-derived by whoever reads this repo. The
# derived crops stay out: they are large and reproducible from that clip.

# Real footage and calibration - large, and reproduced from the dataset / your own capture
data/zerowaste/
data/zerowaste_gt/
data/zerowaste_crops/
# NB: this also hides the locally generated checkerboard_9x6.png. That is intended -
# the .pdf is committed, and tools/make_checkerboard.py regenerates the .png.
data/checkerboard/*.png
data/checkerboard/*.jpg
!data/checkerboard/checkerboard_9x6.pdf
module_B_calibration/calibration.npz
# The unsorted crop dump is an intermediate no code path reads - crops/unsorted/ is regenerated by
# module_E_recognition/extract_crops.py. The SORTED crops/ (the labelled set recognize.py trains on)
# IS committed, because those labels are a human artifact that nobody else could reproduce.
module_E_recognition/raw_crops/

# Jupyter checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.*/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
~$*

# Archives
*.zip
# annotated frames of the dataset clip - regenerate locally, do not commit
reference_grid.png
reference_marked.png

# Windows Explorer folder metadata, one per directory on Windows - never part of the project
desktop.ini

# Ad-hoc screenshots dropped into the repo root (the deliverable images live in outputs/ and are
# committed). Leading slash keeps this root-only so module output PNGs are unaffected.
/Screenshot *.png
